{title: It Is Well with My Soul}
{artist: Horatio Spafford}
{key: C}
{tempo: 72}
{time: 4/4}

{start_of_verse: Verse 1}
When [C]peace like a [F]river at[C]tendeth my way,
When [C]sorrows like [Am]sea billows [D7]roll;[G]
What[C]ever my [F]lot, thou hast [C]taught me to say,
It is [F]well, it is [G7]well with my [C]soul.
{end_of_verse}

{start_of_chorus}
It is [G]well (it is well)
With my [C]soul (with my soul),
It is [F]well, it is [G7]well with my [C]soul.
{end_of_chorus}
